<title>The tangent line as a linear approximation</title>
<p><ref>Video</ref> | <ref>Transcript</ref></p>
<description>
How the tangent line to the graph of a function is a linear approximation to the function close by the tangent point.
</description>


<section name="vid_section"><title>Video</title>
<figure suppressFigureNameInCaption="true">
<video youtube="PC4f3XzK2bc" size="large" aspectRatio="16/9" name="v1" />
<caption>The tangent line as a linear approximation</caption>
</figure>

<setup>
  <number name="timestamp1">60</number>
  <number name="timestamp2">295</number>
</setup>
  

